17592186425751 1079 #uuid "5943d631-1c0b-56a0-a90d-e9d31d030f54" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425752 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425732 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425752 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425734 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425752 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425737 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425752 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425742 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425752 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425746 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425752 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425752 1077 "selection" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425752 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425734 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425752 1079 #uuid "5fa84345-5063-5b45-a9a8-f4e3ac36fb05" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425753 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425752 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425753 1069 "q-143424" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425753 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425753 1071 "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{8}$ is a sample of size $n=8$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =30$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=16,$ calculate the standard error of $\\overset{―}{X}.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425753 1072 #uuid "27d2a840-69cf-5325-b960-367fa82827bd" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425753 1074 "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nSince the population variance is ${\\sigma }^{2}=16$ and the sample size is $n=8,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}] & =\\frac{16}{8} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{2}≈1.41.\n$$" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425754 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425751 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425754 1069 "q-143423" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425754 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425754 1071 "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{20}$ is a sample of size $n=20$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =6$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=1,$ calculate the standard error of $\\overset{―}{X}.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425754 1072 #uuid "748a2779-e90d-59a2-9916-b0ad2a8182a7" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425754 1074 "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nSince the population variance is ${\\sigma }^{2}=1$ and the sample size is $n=20,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}] & =\\frac{1}{20} \\\\  & =0.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{0.05}≈0.22.\n$$" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425755 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425750 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425755 1069 "q-143486" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425755 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425755 1071 "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ of $n$ bushes is drawn from a population. The population has bushes of two different heights, $4\\,\\text{ft}$ and $5\\,\\text{ft},$ distributed in the ratio $3:2.$ Determine the smallest sample size required so that the standard error of the mean is less than $0.01\\,\\text{ft}.$" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425755 1072 #uuid "d1b6912a-93b9-571b-8ea5-2d8ab50d8a7a" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425755 1074 "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the bushes in the population have heights $4\\,\\text{ft}$ and $5\\,\\text{ft},$ and these are distributed in the ratio $3:2.$ Therefore, to compute the population's mean and variance, we can consider a population consisting of $3+2=5$ bushes only with the following heights:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\text{ft},\\,4\\,\\text{ft},\\,4\\,\\text{ft},\\,5\\,\\text{ft},\\,5\\,\\text{ft}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(12+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{22}{5} \\\\  & =4.4\\,\\text{ft},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}^{2}-{\\mu }^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(3\\cdot {4}^{2}+2\\cdot {5}^{2})-{4.4}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(98)-19.36 \\\\  & =19.6-19.36 \\\\  & =0.24\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the population standard deviation is $\\sigma =\\sqrt{0.24},$ and we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\frac{0.24}{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe require that the standard error is less than $0.01\\,\\text{ft}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{0.24}{n}} & <0.01 \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\frac{\\sqrt{0.24}}{0.01} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\sqrt{\\frac{0.24}{{0.01}^{2}}} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\sqrt{2\\,400} \\\\ n & >2\\,400.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest sample size is $n=2\\,401.$" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425756 1058 #edb/ref 17592186425759 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425756 1062 #uuid "26fcd0c3-24b3-5951-9b42-4462bd2fac3d" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425756 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162382 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425757 1058 #edb/ref 17592186425760 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425757 1062 #uuid "3e79243e-67ec-56e0-9d13-5331e6398a52" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425757 1063 #edb/ref 17592186425753 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425758 1062 #uuid "a723e053-b0fa-5616-b5a2-e66027d73c57" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425758 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162394 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425759 1058 #edb/ref 17592186425757 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425759 1062 #uuid "c77ffddd-aed2-56b6-b329-53374af11408" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425759 1063 #edb/ref 17592186425754 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425760 1058 #edb/ref 17592186425758 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425760 1062 #uuid "fe9fb3ff-fe13-546b-ad08-eeb0688c4db2" 13194139534560 17592186045417 true] [17592186425760 1063 #edb/ref 17592186425755 13194139534560 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-7fa56d66-b299-55c7-8a43-47f002ff063b" 17592186425729 "answer-0a2ebf1d-6b21-517e-8473-6b5520ced24c" 17592186425730 "answer-0e7b64bf-b6ca-57e9-aaa1-181aed3d622b" 17592186425731 "answer-116200b8-f0e0-5d54-986b-cdb0d1f93684" 17592186425732 "answer-160f3d12-5eab-5995-9f63-e81fe88512ce" 17592186425733 "answer-19e33d38-75d1-531e-92cf-f39947aea28c" 17592186425734 "answer-210567c7-e894-5b02-9ee8-c6893172df38" 17592186425735 "answer-25a99cc8-8701-579f-b7ef-cb9e7b7f1e7c" 17592186425736 "answer-3e89daf0-19fa-53f4-b72d-31d6ed1621bb" 17592186425737 "answer-55e8daa5-4432-5f7f-b7b9-25ac21b5f238" 17592186425738 "ans